# arthurpower workflow (resident)

This rule is the **always-on router**. Full procedures live in `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and subagent briefs in `.cursor/agents/`. Vendor pin: `.cursor/vendor/arthurpower/VERSION`.

Do **not** start `skill-authoring`, `self-evolving-rules`, or `setup-arthurpower` unless the operator named them. Those are not vendored here.

## Current slot only

Name the task class, then run **one** skill. Documented sequences are ordered gates — do not stack SPECIFY + ACR + PLAN + review in one turn. Competing skills in the same slot (ACR vs `code-review`) are not a sequence: pick one.

## Flowchart

SSOT for the full tree is `.cursor/skills/using-agent-skills/references/flowchart.md`. The copy below omits meta authoring (`skill-authoring` / `self-evolving-rules` / `setup-arthurpower`). If they disagree, follow the skill file.

```
Task arrives
│
├── Scale router (sequence — invoke the current slot only)
│   ├── Scope 已定 + single session ─────────→ logicsync
│   ├── Scope 已定 + multi-session ──────────→ architecture-change-reviewer → writing-plans
│   └── Scope 未定 + multi-session ──────────→ architecture-change-reviewer → writing-plans
│                                              (session-handoff when the session must persist)
│
├── Defining what to build
│   ├── Vague / under-specified request ──→ logicsync
│   ├── Glossary / ADR / SSOT decision ───→ domain-modeling
│   ├── Don't know what you want yet ────→ logicsync
│   ├── Have rough concept, need variants → wayfinder
│   └── New project/feature/change ───────→ spec-driven-development
│
├── Planning implementation
│   ├── Spec ready, ACR not yet / not yes ─→ architecture-change-reviewer
│   ├── ACR all-yes, next artifact is plan → writing-plans
│   └── Single-file or trivial ──────────→ minimal-change-verifier
│
├── Implementing code
│   ├── TDD: failing test first ──────────→ test-driven-development
│   ├── 5-class boundary contract ────────→ defensive-contract-validator
│   ├── Module boundary violation ───────→ bounded-context-guardian
│   ├── Complexity threshold breach ─────→ complexity-anti-drift
│   └── Empty catch / null-on-failure ───→ error-handling-enforcer
│
├── Verifying
│   ├── Bug / something broke ───────────→ systematic-debugging
│   └── Pre-merge final check ──────────→ verification-before-completion
│
├── Reviewing
│   ├── Pre-impl 5-verdict ─────────────→ architecture-change-reviewer
│   └── Post-impl dual-axis review ──────→ code-review
│
├── Committing / branching
│   └── 1 commit = 1 logical task ──────→ minimal-change-verifier
│
└── Meta / orchestration
    └── 2+ independent tasks to fan out → dispatching-parallel-agents
        (current agent runs the skill; workers do the work)
```

`architecture-change-reviewer` blocks on any `no` / `unclear`. `writing-plans` and `spec-driven-development` are user-invoked gates that the router may still open as the **current sequence slot**. `dispatching-parallel-agents` is model-invoked: this agent fans out workers.

## After classify: open the skill file

Follow `.cursor/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` and its `references/`. Do not improvise a shorter procedure.

`code-review`: dispatch `.cursor/agents/standards-reviewer-agent.md` and `.cursor/agents/spec-reviewer-agent.md` in parallel (Standards + Spec). Other S1–S6 / ACR / TDD / boundary-testing agents live in the same directory.

Git commit shape: `.cursor/skills/using-agent-skills/references/git-workflow.md` plus `minimal-change-verifier`.

